  * imperfect, at-most-once guarantee. This favors never double-applying a
  * side-effect (e.g. double-grading a job) over guaranteeing every item
  * eventually completes; a side-effect that fails AFTER its marker is written
- * is reported in the outcome line and will NOT be retried automatically —
- * the same "écart" reporting path (or a human) is expected to catch it.
+ * is reported in the outcome line.
+ *
+ * What happens next depends on `r.kind` — see `RETRYABLE_ON_FAILURE_KINDS`
+ * just below. For the kinds NOT in that set (today: `skillJobGrade`,
+ * `sessionReview`), the marker is left in place but its `status` is
+ * overwritten to `'failed'` (see `cmdImport`'s catch block) so the file no
+ * longer lies by claiming `'applying'` forever — it stays sealed, and the
+ * same "écart" reporting path (or a human) is expected to catch it.
  */
 async function writeMarker(p: string, resultsSha: string, itemKey: string, status: string): Promise<void> {
   await atomicWrite(p, JSON.stringify({ resultsSha, itemKey, status, importedAt: new Date().toISOString() }, null, 2));
 }

+/**
+ * `r.kind` values whose side-effect (`applyResultSideEffects`) is PROVEN to
+ * leave nothing behind when it fails mid-execution — so removing the marker
+ * on failure and letting a later `cmdImport` retry the item is safe (never
+ * double-applies a partial mutation). Verified by reading every branch of
+ * `applyResultSideEffects` (see the enumeration table in the commit this
+ * constant was introduced in, or `evalsReconciler.test.ts`'s retry tests):
+ *
+ * - `improvementDiff` — self-cleaning: the `catch` best-effort `rm`s any
+ *   diff/backup artifact THIS attempt wrote, and `createGatedProposal`
+ *   (apply.ts) itself deletes the hub gate conversation it just wrote if
+ *   creating the `ImprovementProposal` afterwards fails (fix from an
+ *   adversarial review predating this constant). A git branch push, if it
+ *   happened, is itself idempotent (`transportImproveBranch` no-ops when the
+ *   branch is already up to date).
+ *
+ * Deliberately NOT included, despite reading as idempotent on a first pass
+ * (`skillJobGrade`'s `updateSkillJob` / `sessionReview`'s `updateSessionStamp`
+ * are single atomic, optimistic-locked, full-overwrite writes — no
+ * accumulation) — `writeMarker`'s own docstring calls out "double-grading a
+ * job" as the exact risk this at-most-once guarantee exists to prevent, and
+ * that call was never subjected to the same adversarial scrutiny
+ * `improvementDiff` got. Sealing them on failure (status `'failed'`, never
+ * retried automatically) keeps today's behavior unless a future lot proves
+ * them safe with the same rigor and adds them here.
+ *
+ * `note` never reaches this decision at all — its `applyResultSideEffects`
+ * branch is a pure no-op (no I/O), so it can never throw and never lands in
+ * `cmdImport`'s catch block.
+ */
+const RETRYABLE_ON_FAILURE_KINDS: ReadonlySet<ImportResultItem['kind']> = new Set(['improvementDiff']);
+
 /* -------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
 /*  Scope-lint (protection against a toxic improve/<skill> diff)              */
 /* -------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
@@ -2913,16 +2951,41 @@ export async function cmdImport(opts: { dryRun: boolean; from?: string; date?: s
         outcomes.push(`${itemKey} : ingéré (${r.kind})`);
       } catch (err) {
